---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Methods · Recovery Observatory">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methods</p>
      <h1>From event boundary to recovery trajectory.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The observatory is designed around reproducible spatial comparison:
        define the disaster geography, normalize indicators, trace temporal
        change, and interpret recovery through ecological, socioeconomic,
        demographic, social, and policy evidence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid two">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Spatial Frame</h3>
          <p>
            Establish a disaster boundary, affected administrative units, and
            comparable spatial grids or zones. Future versions can add GeoJSON
            layers for intensity, damage, relocation, planning, and land-cover
            change.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Temporal Frame</h3>
          <p>
            Store annual or milestone observations to distinguish emergency
            response, reconstruction, stabilization, and long-run transformation.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Indicator Harmonization</h3>
          <p>
            Keep raw data transparent, then derive comparable measures using
            consistent units, time windows, spatial aggregation, and uncertainty
            notes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Mixed Evidence</h3>
          <p>
            Combine remote sensing, census and statistical data, policy texts,
            news, social media, planning documents, field observations, and
            interviews when available.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
